{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Nanda: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja39'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 39 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Kulāvakavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nests </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>9. Nandajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Nanda: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Maññe sovaṇṇayo rāsi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>I suspect the heap of gold </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>soṇṇamālā ca nandako; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and golden chains </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yattha dāso āmajāto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>is where the house-born slave Nandaka </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ṭhito thullāni gajjatī”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>stands yelling curses. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Nandajātakaṁ navamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
